    "stem": "Imran fills three cells in a row with numbers. A cell is a supercell when its number is greater than each immediate neighbour. He wants only the left cell to be a supercell.\n\nWhich statements are correct?",
    "item_type": "three_statement",
    "options": {
      "A": "1 only",
      "B": "1 and 2 only",
      "C": "2 and 3 only",
      "D": "1, 2 and 3"
    },
    "statements": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "text": "The filling $9$, $5$, $3$ works, because only the left cell is greater than its immediate neighbour."
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "text": "Any filling where $9$ appears is enough, because $9$ is the intended supercell label."
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "text": "The supercell rule is produced by first labelling the left cell as intended, without comparing $9$ with $5$."
      }
